    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d114">

                <pb facs="0231" n="161" xml:id="pg161"/>

                <head>Mr. Adams to Mr. Seward.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 198.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">London,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1862-07-31"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >July</hi> 31, 1862.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have the honor to transmit copies of two
                    more notes, which have been exchanged here since my last despatch, (No. 188,)
                    touching the case of the United States steamer Saginaw and her warning to leave
                    the port of Hong Kong.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>CHARLES FRANCIS ADAMS.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of State, Washington, D. C.</hi></p>
                </postscript>



                <xi:include href="d114-a1.xml" xpointer="d114-a1"/>
